on-ending surgery on arm","description":"Texas starting defensive tackle Hero Kanu had season-ending surgery on his arm Monday, coach Steve Sarkisian announced.","published":"2026-11-16T20:55:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503942/texas-dl-hero-kanu-undergoes-season-ending-surgery-arm","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Cignetti: Narrative surrounding Indiana serves as motivation","description":"Indiana coach Curt Cignetti thinks his team's accomplishments continue to be unfairly discredited, and he's using it for motivation as the Hoosiers chase another national title.","published":"2026-11-16T19:38:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503441/narrative-surrounding-indiana-serves-motivation","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":8,"round":1,"team":"ATL","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:53Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}